WHAT THIS PATCH IS, AND WHAT REVIEW r1 CHANGED IN IT
----------------------------------------------------

The brief's original §6 H6 was a one-line import swap plus `nativeTrendContext:
trendBinding.resolve`. Review r1 accepted the mechanism and rejected the form on
three counts. All three are fixed here:

  (a) NAMED IMPORTS FROM A CommonJS MODULE (review §5.1, "style defect").
      gym-host.mjs states its own rule two lines above the import block:
      "CommonJS collaborators are taken as DEFAULT imports, the way the accepted
      host entry (rebuild/m3/w6/host/host-entry.mjs) takes them". Every other CJS
      collaborator in the file — Source, Capture, Commands, Adapter, History,
      SourceProjection, WorkoutBasis, ResumePolicy, HostRuntime, T2Stage,
      Canonical — is a default import. The original hunk broke that rule and
      worked only while `module.exports = { … }` stays an object literal
      cjs-module-lexer can read. This patch takes the DEFAULT import and
      destructures beside the file's other destructures.

  (b) THE BIND WINDOW (review F3 / C3). gym-model.readPrevious()
      (gym-model.mjs:128-139) re-runs the accepted reader over the reconstructed
      lastProjection() input AFTER workoutProducer has returned. With a window
      that lived only inside the producer, that read threw
      PERFORMED_NATIVE_TREND_CONTEXT_REQUIRED / resolver_failed,
      gym-model.mjs:136 swallowed it, and the card showed NO previous
      performance on exactly the days B-NTC unblocks. This patch moves the
      window onto the engine handle: every engine read over a state that carries
      its own workoutFacts runs inside `binding.withFacts(facts, …)`, which is
      bind … finally RESTORE and is re-entrant, so the producer's own window is
      not disarmed by a nested read. Measured both ways in D6 / D6-control below.

  (c) THE S2 OPTION, OFF BY DEFAULT (review F2 / C2, PM question Q1).
      `mapRecordedDaysWithEnginePredicates` is a new createGymHost option,
      default FALSE, and the shipped page passes nothing, so the page behaves
      exactly as it does today. It has an effect only when BOTH it is true AND
      the runtime exposes dayWeather + cleanAtDate — which no accepted runtime
      does, because EXPOSED is ['genSession','rirPlan'] and that list is pinned
      by native-carriers-witnesses.cjs:16. `trendDayReader()` reports which
      reader was composed so a caller states the truth instead of assuming it.

